# {{.Service}}

Kitex service generated by devkit.

```sh
make tools        # once per machine: kitex + thriftgo
make gen          # regenerate kitex_gen/ from the IDLs listed in idl.mk
make run          # APP_ENV=dev, no Nacos required
make test
```

- IDL lives in the project's shared IDL repository (`../idl` next to this
  service). Change it there, run `make gen`, implement new methods in
  `handler/`, and open a pull request in the IDL repository.
- To call another service, add its IDL to `idl.mk` (for example
  `order/order.thrift`), run `make gen`, and use the generated client in
  `kitex_gen/`. `idl.mk` is yours; devkit never rewrites it.
- Configuration is `conf/<APP_ENV>.yaml`; `${VAR}` placeholders are read from
  the environment.
- Shared infrastructure (logging, Nacos, Redis, ...) comes from
  `{{.CommonModule}}`.
